---
title: Network Architecture
---

sequenceDiagram
    participant M as Main Thread
    participant C as Client Thread
    participant S as Server Thread

    note over M: User clicks "Server"
    M->>S: startServerThread()
    note over S: binds TCP port 8080<br/>waits for connections

    note over M: User clicks "Client"
    M->>C: networkClientConnect("ip")
    note over C: clientRunning = 1

    C->>S: TCP connect on port 8080
    S->>C: NetWelcomePacket { magic, playerId }
    note over C: clientConnected = 1<br/>clientPlayerId = N

    loop every ~8ms (server tick)

        note over M: SDL_GetKeyboardState()
        M->>M: networkClientSetInput(l,r,u,d)
        note over M: 🔒 mutex<br/>write clientInput<br/>🔓 mutex

        note over C: 🔒 mutex<br/>copy clientInput<br/>🔓 mutex
        C->>S: NetInputPacket { magic, left, right, up, down }

        note over S: updateServerGame()<br/>─ move players<br/>─ fire bullets every 10 ticks<br/>─ move bullets & enemies<br/>─ bullet↔enemy collisions → score<br/>─ player↔enemy collisions → lives

        S->>C: NetGameState { players[], bullets[], enemies[],<br/>lives, score, gameOver, playerId, connectedPlayers }

        note over C: 🔒 mutex<br/>write clientState<br/>🔓 mutex

        M->>M: networkClientGetState(&state)
        note over M: 🔒 mutex<br/>copy clientState<br/>🔓 mutex

        M->>M: render(state)
    end

    note over M: gameOver or disconnect
    M->>C: networkClientDisconnect()
    note over C: clientRunning = 0<br/>close socket
    note over S: detects client gone<br/>removes from slot
